ee scales have different lengths, so before combining them, normalize each score. A four-level scale returns 0 to 3 and a three-level scale returns 0 to 2, so a top score on one is bigger than a top score on the other. Divide each score by its top level number, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`len(criteria) - 1`}),`, to put every score on 0 to 1. Then the weights mean what they say: 0.6 on severity and 0.3 on frustration makes severity count twice as much.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`The TypeSafe Python SDK code below asks the three questions, normalizes each score, and combines them using an example priority calculation:`}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLines:`51`,language:`python`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`python`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`python`,numberOfLines:`51`,children:[_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#CF222E`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#C586C0`},children:`from`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:` typesafe_sdk `}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#CF222E`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#C586C0`},children:`import`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:` Score, TypeSafeClient`})]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0550AE`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:`TRIAGE_QUESTIONS`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#CF222E`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:` =`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:` {`})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#0A3069`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#CE9178`},children:`    